The embedding model is openWakeWord's port of Google's speech_embedding
model (https://tfhub.dev/google/speech_embedding/1), Apache License 2.0.
It runs here, on the robot's computer: no request ever leaves it.

Converted unchanged (float32), by the plan in kws.Features; the numbers
match onnxruntime's to 1e-6 (robot/tests/test_brain_kws.py).

The voices `brain wake` learns from (robot/brain/voices.py) are made on the
robot's computer with edge-tts (Microsoft's neural voices) and stay there.
